{
 "scene_id": "01.4",
 "poem": "01",
 "title": "Out of Life",
 "movement": "AS DARK AS BLACK",
 "seconds": 14,
 "lines": "crashing the party / of your evilest instincts / to find vibrations / that echo in silence\u2014 / love & hate languages / that translate in / slow dripping blood / salivating on / imminent doubts\u2014 / fully awakening / to our darkest night. / pause for a second / a spectrum of / feels\u2014will threads / needles of garments / made of / sweet memories\u2014 / in photographs, / film & fiction that / leave me empty. / with your back / faced against me\u2014 / you offer me a new / pursuit of happiness / as I stumble / on my own words, / landing into / the secret of\u2014 / where you go when you / leave\u2014 / & I fall out of life.",
